 c004 branch.\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":2,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":[" {\"candidate_id\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"440a75f0da4810d3d3c5c83adc62c95f0f06cc9677b061798df439273e835d62\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Faithful Option-A 4-kernel SSD (K1 chunk_cumsum, K2 chunk_state, K3 state_passing, K4 chunk_scan); fp32 accumulation everywhere, tl.dot input_precision='ieee' on all matmuls. Correctness-first baseline to lock all five workloads.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"initial implementation\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (strides/masks/cumsum axis/exp-difference order/dtypes/K3 recurrence & K4 Y_diag+Y_off+D algebra re-derived vs reference; all tl.dot tile shapes have K>=16 and M,N>=16)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"all_passed\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 workloads RUNTIME_ERROR (uniform, non-tolerance). Kernel compile/launch failure, not algebra. Leading suspects: (a) tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') kwarg unsupported on the installed Triton build (older Triton uses allow_tf32=); (b) fp32 tl.dot on large [64,256]/[256,64] tiles overflowing A800 shared memory with default pipelining/num_warps=8. Harness exposes no traceback; could not probe triton version (bash python blocked by sandbox).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 1, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Next c002: remove input_precision kwarg entirely and feed bf16 operands into every tl.dot (fp32 accumulation kept by default), which both sidesteps the kwarg-compat risk and halves dot-operand SRAM; keep decays/exp/cumsum/accumulators/D-residual in fp32; add explicit num_warps=4, num_stages=2 to bound SRAM. K1-K4 algebra unchanged (verified).\"}","-{\"candidate_id\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_sha256\": \"0b2cf934a0efdafdd94ec935835da2001dcdf74ae85e1eecb4985b5c41686293\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:30:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"c001 failed to launch (all RUNTIME_ERROR). Feed bf16 operands into every tl.dot with default fp32 accumulation and drop the input_precision kwarg; pin num_warps=4/num_stages=2. This removes kwarg-compat risk and halves dot-operand SRAM while keeping all decays/exp/cumsum/accumulators/D-residual in fp32. Expect all 5 to pass and a large speedup over the memory-bound reference.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"All tl.dot now consume bf16 operands (Xd cast to bf16 after fp32 decay in K2; M cast to bf16 after fp32 mask/exp in K4; states_o cast to bf16 for C.states dot); removed input_precision='ieee'; num_warps 8->4 on K2/K4, added num_stages=2 to K2/K4.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (algebra identical to c001; only dot operand dtype + launch params changed)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 10.486993283989488, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.157534, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 12.25298535944318, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.254157, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 8.973383428660055, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.1579655, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 8.939661476559777, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.1593095, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 13.229428499147975, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.209501, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 10.640015419344408, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 10.776490409560095, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 workloads PASS; geomean 10.64x over the memory-bound reference. New best and parent. bf16 tl.dot operands confirmed the c001 failure was compilation/launch (kwarg or SRAM), not algebra. Correctness holds comfortably (bf16 operands == reference operand precision; fp32 accumulation).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 2, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Occupancy pattern as predicted: 64-tile workloads (WL3 L=256 8.97x, WL4 B=1 8.94x) trail the high-parallelism ones (WL2 256-tile 12.25x, WL5 192-tile 13.23x). Next levers: (c003) head-shared G reuse in K4 -- compute C.B^T once per (b,chunk) across all 16 heads (n_groups=1) to cut the diagonal matmul ~16x, and/or expose more grid parallelism for the 64-tile cases. Head-shared G needs restructuring K4 grid to group-major (loop heads inside block) since L/decay is head-dependent but G is not.\"}","+{\"candidate_id\"