{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-883e42ec-0722-435e-9fa4-170ea21f228c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The planned \"in-SRAM head fusion\" (old c004 idea) is now contraindicated: c003 proved c002 is **not** bound by the redundant `C·Bᵀ` matmul, and head fusion would also cut grid parallelism 16× (hurting the low-occupancy cases). Let me reason about the actual bottleneck from the c002 timing vector before implementing.\n\nThe three 64-tile workloads (WL1/3/4) all land at ~0.158 ms regardless of NC∈{1,2,4} or B∈{1,2,4}, while 192-tile=0.210 and 256-tile=0.254. A linear `time ≈ floor + slope·tiles` fit gives **floor ≈ 0.126 ms** (≈80% of the 64-tile runtime) and slope ≈ 0.5 µs/tile. So a large fixed overhead — 4 sequential kernel launches plus the `acum`/`alast` DRAM round-trips — dominates the small cases. The cleanest single lever is to **eliminate K1** by recomputing the cheap 256-element cumsum inside K2/K3/K4, removing one launch and the `acum`+`alast` intermediates."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":106489,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6fba2c0-4823-4806-9479-4c36036ed424","uuid":"7810e422-cab4-453d-9434-0eabd0cdf2dd","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:03:48.924Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-883e42ec-0722-435e-9fa4-170ea21f228c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HuvDiZ2C1eZZrLgq7fv1X1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/solution/solution.py","content":"\"\"\"L2/043 Mamba-2 chunk scan with segment sum — Triton solution.\n\nCandidate c004: fuse the K1 cumsum kernel away (recompute in K2/K3/K4).\n\nEvidence driving this change: on c002 (5/5 PASS, geomean 10.64x) the per-workload\ntiming vector shows the three 64-tile workloads (WL1/3/4) all sit at ~0.158 ms regardless\nof NC in {1,2,4} or B in {1,2,4}, while 192-tile=0.210 ms and 256-tile=0.254 ms. A linear\nfit ``time ≈ floor + slope·tiles`` gives floor ≈ 0.126 ms (~80% of the 64-tile runtime) and\nslope ≈ 0.5 us/tile — i.e. a large fixed overhead (4 kernel launches + the acum/alast DRAM\nround-trips) dominates the small cases. c003 already showed c002 is NOT bound by redundant\nG = C·Bᵀ matmul, so the right lever is cutting fixed overhead, not matmul FLOPs.\n\nThis candidate removes kernel K1 entirely: the per-chunk cumsum a[t] = cumsum_t A and its\ntotal a_last are recomputed inside K2, K3 and K4 (a[t] is a cheap 256-element scan). That\ndeletes one launch and the ``acum:[B,H,NC,Q]`` + ``alast:[B,H,NC]`` DRAM tensors (read\ntwice, written once). Algebra is unchanged and numerically identical to c002 (cumsum in\nfp32; padded rows load A=0 so the scan stays flat, matching the reference). In K4 the query\n/ key cumsum sub-blocks a_i / a_j are extracted from the full fp32 cumsum via an exact\none-hot gather (a [BLOCK_M, Q] mask-and-sum, negligible next to the matmuls).\n\nAll decays / cumsum / exp / accumulators / D residual stay in fp32; bf16 only for\ntensor-core operands and the final output / final_state casts.\n\nStages (all working intermediates in fp32; only output / final_state cast to bf16):\n  K2 chunk_state    : a=cumsum(A); states[p,n] = sum_t exp(a_last - a[t]) * X[t,p] * B[t,n].\n  K3 state_passing  : a_last(c)=sum_t A; recurrence seeded by initial_states,\n                      new_states[c+1] = exp(a_last(c)) * new_states[c] + states[c];\n                      states_out[c] = new_states[c], final_state = new_states[NC].\n  K4 chunk_scan     : a=cumsum(A); Y = (G∘L)·X + exp(a[t])·(C·states_out) + D[h]·X,\n                      G[i,j]=C_i·B_j, L[i,j]=exp(a[i]-a[j]) lower-tri; no [Q,Q] to DRAM.\n\nConstants for this task: H=16, P=64, N=256, n_groups=1, Q(chunk)=256.\nNo Torch/CPU/NumPy computational fallback anywhere: Triton is the only compute path.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K2: per-(b,chunk,head) state = sum_t decay_state[t] * X[t,:] outer B[t,:].\n#     grid = (B*NC*H, N // BLOCK_N).  Recomputes a = cumsum(A) inline.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _chunk_state_kernel(\n    X_ptr, B_ptr, A_ptr, states_ptr,\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    bch = tl.program_id(0)\n    nblk = tl.program_id(1)\n    b = bch // (NC * H)\n    rem = bch % (NC * H)\n    c = rem // H\n    h = rem % H\n\n    t = tl.arange(0, Q)\n    seq = c * Q + t\n    tmask = seq < L\n    p = tl.arange(0, P)\n    n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n\n    Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=tmask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    acum = tl.cumsum(Arow, axis=0)          # [Q]\n    alast = tl.sum(Arow, axis=0)            # scalar\n    decay = tl.exp(alast - acum)            # [Q]\n\n    X = tl.load(\n        X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + p[None, :] * sX_p,\n        mask=tmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    ).to(tl.float32)  # [Q, P]\n    Xd = (X * decay[:, None]).to(tl.bfloat16)  # [Q, P] bf16 (decay applied in fp32)\n\n    Bt = tl.load(\n        B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq[:, None] * sB_l + n[None, :] * sB_n,\n        mask=tmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    )  # [Q, BLOCK_N] bf16 (native)\n\n    states = tl.dot(tl.trans(Xd), Bt)  # [P, BLOCK_N] fp32 accumulate\n    tl.store(\n        states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n,\n        states,\n    )\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K3: inter-chunk sequential recurrence. grid = (B, H, N // BLOCK_N).\n#     Recomputes a_last(c) = sum_t A inline (no alast tensor).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _state_passing_kernel(\n    states_ptr, init_ptr, states_out_ptr, final_ptr, A_ptr,\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n    si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n    sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    b = tl.program_id(0)\n    h = tl.program_id(1)\n    nblk = tl.program_id(2)\n\n    p = tl.arange(0, P)\n    n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n    t = tl.arange(0, Q)\n\n    state = tl.load(\n        init_ptr + b * si_b + h * si_h + p[:, None] * si_p + n[None, :] * si_n\n    ).to(tl.float32)  # [P, BLOCK_N]\n\n    for c in range(0, NC):\n        tl.store(\n            states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + p[:, None] * so_p + n[None, :] * so_n,\n            state,\n        )\n        seq = c * Q + t\n        smask = seq < L\n        Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=smask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n        g = tl.exp(tl.sum(Arow, axis=0))\n        st = tl.load(\n            states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n\n        ).to(tl.float32)\n        state = g * state + st\n\n    tl.store(\n        final_ptr + b * sf_b + h * sf_h + p[:, None] * sf_p + n[None, :] * sf_n,\n        state.to(tl.bfloat16),\n    )\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K4: chunk scan. grid = (B*NC*H, Q // BLOCK_M).  Recomputes a = cumsum(A) inline.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _chunk_scan_kernel(\n    C_ptr, B_ptr, X_ptr, A_ptr, states_out_ptr, D_ptr, out_ptr,\n    sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n    sD_h,\n    sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    bch = tl.program_id(0)\n    iblk = tl.program_id(1)\n    b = bch // (NC * H)\n    rem = bch % (NC * H)\n    c = rem // H\n    h = rem % H\n\n    qidx = tl.arange(0, Q)\n    seq_full = c * Q + qidx\n    fmask = seq_full < L\n    Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq_full * sA_l, mask=fmask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    a_full = tl.cumsum(Arow, axis=0)  # [Q]\n\n    im = iblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)  # chunk-local query rows\n    seq_i = c * Q + im\n    imask = seq_i < L\n    nidx = tl.arange(0, N)\n    pidx = tl.arange(0, P)\n\n    # exact gather a_i = a_full[im] via one-hot mask-sum\n    a_i = tl.sum(tl.where(qidx[None, :] == im[:, None], a_full[None, :], 0.0), axis=1)  # [BLOCK_M]\n\n    C_i = tl.load(\n        C_ptr + b * sC_b + seq_i[:, None] * sC_l + nidx[None, :] * sC_n,\n        mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    )  # [BLOCK_M, N] bf16\n\n    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, P), dtype=tl.float32)\n\n    for jblk in range(0, iblk + 1):\n        jm = jblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\n        seq_j = c * Q + jm\n        jmask = seq_j < L\n        a_j = tl.sum(tl.where(qidx[None, :] == jm[:, None], a_full[None, :], 0.0), axis=1)  # [BLOCK_M]\n        B_j = tl.load(\n            B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq_j[:, None] * sB_l + nidx[None, :] * sB_n,\n            mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n        )  # [BLOCK_M, N] bf16\n        X_j = tl.load(\n            X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq_j[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + pidx[None, :] * sX_p,\n            mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n        )  # [BLOCK_M, P] bf16\n\n        G = tl.dot(C_i, tl.trans(B_j))  # [BLOCK_M, BLOCK_M] fp32\n        diff = a_i[:, None] - a_j[None, :]\n        cmask = im[:, None] >= jm[None, :]\n        Lm = tl.where(cmask, tl.exp(diff), 0.0)\n        M = (G * Lm).to(tl.bfloat16)\n        acc += tl.dot(M, X_j)\n\n    states_o = tl.load(\n        states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + pidx[:, None] * so_p + nidx[None, :] * so_n\n    ).to(tl.bfloat16)  # [P, N]\n    Cstate = tl.dot(C_i, tl.trans(states_o))  # [BLOCK_M, P] fp32\n    a_i_exp = tl.exp(a_i)\n    Y = acc + a_i_exp[:, None] * Cstate\n\n    X_i = tl.load(\n        X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq_i[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + pidx[None, :] * sX_p,\n        mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    ).to(tl.float32)\n    Dh = tl.load(D_ptr + h * sD_h).to(tl.float32)\n    Y = Y + Dh * X_i\n\n    out_off = out_ptr + b * sout_b + seq_i[:, None] * sout_l + (h * P + pidx[None, :]) * sout_hp\n    tl.store(out_off, Y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=imask[:, None])\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Host entry point.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef run(hidden_states, A, B, C, D, initial_states):\n    Bb, L, H, P = hidden_states.shape\n    N = 256\n    Q = 256\n    device = hidden_states.device\n\n    pad = (Q - L % Q) % Q\n    L_pad = L + pad\n    NC = L_pad // Q\n\n    BLOCK_M = 64\n    BLOCK_N = 64\n\n    states = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    states_out = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    final_state = torch.empty((Bb, H, P, N), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)\n    output = torch.empty((Bb, L, H * P), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)\n\n    # strides\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l = A.stride(0), A.stride(1), A.stride(2)\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p = hidden_states.stride()\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n = B.stride(0), B.stride(1), B.stride(3)\n    sC_b, sC_l, sC_n = C.stride(0), C.stride(1), C.stride(3)\n    sD_h = D.stride(0)\n    si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n = initial_states.stride()\n\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n = states.stride()\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n = states_out.stride()\n    sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n = final_state.stride()\n    sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp = output.stride()\n\n    # K2: chunk_state (recomputes cumsum inline)\n    _chunk_state_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, N // BLOCK_N)](\n        hidden_states, B, A, states,\n        sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n        sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,\n    )\n\n    # K3: state_passing (recomputes a_last inline)\n    _state_passing_kernel[(Bb, H, N // BLOCK_N)](\n        states, initial_states, states_out, final_state, A,\n        sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n        si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,\n        so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n        sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4,\n    )\n\n    # K4: chunk_scan (recomputes cumsum inline)\n    _chunk_scan_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, Q // BLOCK_M)](\n        C, B, hidden_states, A, states_out, D, output,\n        sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,\n        sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n        sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n        sD_h,\n        sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_M=BLOCK_M, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,\n    )\n\n    return output, final_state\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":106489,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6fba2c0-4823-4806-9479-4c36036ed424","uuid":"3fc49107-a321-4c5a-9b6a-db2c90e48f9f","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:03:48.927Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HuvDiZ2C1eZZrLgq7fv1X1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/solution/solution.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6fba2c0-4823-4806-9479-4c36036ed424","uuid":"5ea4d25a-a333-471d-ad64-3136e9799f61","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:03:48.953Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/solution/solution.py","content":"\"\"\"L2/043 Mamba-2 chunk scan with segment sum — Triton solution.\n\nCandidate c004: fuse the K1 cumsum kernel away (recompute in K2/K3/K4).\n\nEvidence driving this change: on c002 (5/5 PASS, geomean 10.64x) the per-workload\ntiming vector shows the three 64-tile workloads (WL1/3/4) all sit at ~0.158 ms regardless\nof NC in {1,2,4} or B in {1,2,4}, while 192-tile=0.210 ms and 256-tile=0.254 ms. A linear\nfit ``time ≈ floor + slope·tiles`` gives floor ≈ 0.126 ms (~80% of the 64-tile runtime) and\nslope ≈ 0.5 us/tile — i.e. a large fixed overhead (4 kernel launches + the acum/alast DRAM\nround-trips) dominates the small cases. c003 already showed c002 is NOT bound by redundant\nG = C·Bᵀ matmul, so the right lever is cutting fixed overhead, not matmul FLOPs.\n\nThis candidate removes kernel K1 entirely: the per-chunk cumsum a[t] = cumsum_t A and its\ntotal a_last are recomputed inside K2, K3 and K4 (a[t] is a cheap 256-element scan). That\ndeletes one launch and the ``acum:[B,H,NC,Q]`` + ``alast:[B,H,NC]`` DRAM tensors (read\ntwice, written once). Algebra is unchanged and numerically identical to c002 (cumsum in\nfp32; padded rows load A=0 so the scan stays flat, matching the reference). In K4 the query\n/ key cumsum sub-blocks a_i / a_j are extracted from the full fp32 cumsum via an exact\none-hot gather (a [BLOCK_M, Q] mask-and-sum, negligible next to the matmuls).\n\nAll decays / cumsum / exp / accumulators / D residual stay in fp32; bf16 only for\ntensor-core operands and the final output / final_state casts.\n\nStages (all working intermediates in fp32; only output / final_state cast to bf16):\n  K2 chunk_state    : a=cumsum(A); states[p,n] = sum_t exp(a_last - a[t]) * X[t,p] * B[t,n].\n  K3 state_passing  : a_last(c)=sum_t A; recurrence seeded by initial_states,\n                      new_states[c+1] = exp(a_last(c)) * new_states[c] + states[c];\n                      states_out[c] = new_states[c], final_state = new_states[NC].\n  K4 chunk_scan     : a=cumsum(A); Y = (G∘L)·X + exp(a[t])·(C·states_out) + D[h]·X,\n                      G[i,j]=C_i·B_j, L[i,j]=exp(a[i]-a[j]) lower-tri; no [Q,Q] to DRAM.\n\nConstants for this task: H=16, P=64, N=256, n_groups=1, Q(chunk)=256.\nNo Torch/CPU/NumPy computational fallback anywhere: Triton is the only compute path.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K2: per-(b,chunk,head) state = sum_t decay_state[t] * X[t,:] outer B[t,:].\n#     grid = (B*NC*H, N // BLOCK_N).  Recomputes a = cumsum(A) inline.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _chunk_state_kernel(\n    X_ptr, B_ptr, A_ptr, states_ptr,\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    bch = tl.program_id(0)\n    nblk = tl.program_id(1)\n    b = bch // (NC * H)\n    rem = bch % (NC * H)\n    c = rem // H\n    h = rem % H\n\n    t = tl.arange(0, Q)\n    seq = c * Q + t\n    tmask = seq < L\n    p = tl.arange(0, P)\n    n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n\n    Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=tmask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    acum = tl.cumsum(Arow, axis=0)          # [Q]\n    alast = tl.sum(Arow, axis=0)            # scalar\n    decay = tl.exp(alast - acum)            # [Q]\n\n    X = tl.load(\n        X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + p[None, :] * sX_p,\n        mask=tmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    ).to(tl.float32)  # [Q, P]\n    Xd = (X * decay[:, None]).to(tl.bfloat16)  # [Q, P] bf16 (decay applied in fp32)\n\n    Bt = tl.load(\n        B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq[:, None] * sB_l + n[None, :] * sB_n,\n        mask=tmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    )  # [Q, BLOCK_N] bf16 (native)\n\n    states = tl.dot(tl.trans(Xd), Bt)  # [P, BLOCK_N] fp32 accumulate\n    tl.store(\n        states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n,\n        states,\n    )\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K3: inter-chunk sequential recurrence. grid = (B, H, N // BLOCK_N).\n#     Recomputes a_last(c) = sum_t A inline (no alast tensor).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _state_passing_kernel(\n    states_ptr, init_ptr, states_out_ptr, final_ptr, A_ptr,\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n    si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n    sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    b = tl.program_id(0)\n    h = tl.program_id(1)\n    nblk = tl.program_id(2)\n\n    p = tl.arange(0, P)\n    n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n    t = tl.arange(0, Q)\n\n    state = tl.load(\n        init_ptr + b * si_b + h * si_h + p[:, None] * si_p + n[None, :] * si_n\n    ).to(tl.float32)  # [P, BLOCK_N]\n\n    for c in range(0, NC):\n        tl.store(\n            states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + p[:, None] * so_p + n[None, :] * so_n,\n            state,\n        )\n        seq = c * Q + t\n        smask = seq < L\n        Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=smask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n        g = tl.exp(tl.sum(Arow, axis=0))\n        st = tl.load(\n            states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n\n        ).to(tl.float32)\n        state = g * state + st\n\n    tl.store(\n        final_ptr + b * sf_b + h * sf_h + p[:, None] * sf_p + n[None, :] * sf_n,\n        state.to(tl.bfloat16),\n    )\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K4: chunk scan. grid = (B*NC*H, Q // BLOCK_M).  Recomputes a = cumsum(A) inline.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _chunk_scan_kernel(\n    C_ptr, B_ptr, X_ptr, A_ptr, states_out_ptr, D_ptr, out_ptr,\n    sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n    sD_h,\n    sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    bch = tl.program_id(0)\n    iblk = tl.program_id(1)\n    b = bch // (NC * H)\n    rem = bch % (NC * H)\n    c = rem // H\n    h = rem % H\n\n    qidx = tl.arange(0, Q)\n    seq_full = c * Q + qidx\n    fmask = seq_full < L\n    Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq_full * sA_l, mask=fmask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    a_full = tl.cumsum(Arow, axis=0)  # [Q]\n\n    im = iblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)  # chunk-local query rows\n    seq_i = c * Q + im\n    imask = seq_i < L\n    nidx = tl.arange(0, N)\n    pidx = tl.arange(0, P)\n\n    # exact gather a_i = a_full[im] via one-hot mask-sum\n    a_i = tl.sum(tl.where(qidx[None, :] == im[:, None], a_full[None, :], 0.0), axis=1)  # [BLOCK_M]\n\n    C_i = tl.load(\n        C_ptr + b * sC_b + seq_i[:, None] * sC_l + nidx[None, :] * sC_n,\n        mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    )  # [BLOCK_M, N] bf16\n\n    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, P), dtype=tl.float32)\n\n    for jblk in range(0, iblk + 1):\n        jm = jblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\n        seq_j = c * Q + jm\n        jmask = seq_j < L\n        a_j = tl.sum(tl.where(qidx[None, :] == jm[:, None], a_full[None, :], 0.0), axis=1)  # [BLOCK_M]\n        B_j = tl.load(\n            B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq_j[:, None] * sB_l + nidx[None, :] * sB_n,\n            mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n        )  # [BLOCK_M, N] bf16\n        X_j = tl.load(\n            X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq_j[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + pidx[None, :] * sX_p,\n            mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n        )  # [BLOCK_M, P] bf16\n\n        G = tl.dot(C_i, tl.trans(B_j))  # [BLOCK_M, BLOCK_M] fp32\n        diff = a_i[:, None] - a_j[None, :]\n        cmask = im[:, None] >= jm[None, :]\n        Lm = tl.where(cmask, tl.exp(diff), 0.0)\n        M = (G * Lm).to(tl.bfloat16)\n        acc += tl.dot(M, X_j)\n\n    states_o = tl.load(\n        states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + pidx[:, None] * so_p + nidx[None, :] * so_n\n    ).to(tl.bfloat16)  # [P, N]\n    Cstate = tl.dot(C_i, tl.trans(states_o))  # [BLOCK_M, P] fp32\n    a_i_exp = tl.exp(a_i)\n    Y = acc + a_i_exp[:, None] * Cstate\n\n    X_i = tl.load(\n        X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq_i[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + pidx[None, :] * sX_p,\n        mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    ).to(tl.float32)\n    Dh = tl.load(D_ptr + h * sD_h).to(tl.float32)\n    Y = Y + Dh * X_i\n\n    out_off = out_ptr + b * sout_b + seq_i[:, None] * sout_l + (h * P + pidx[None, :]) * sout_hp\n    tl.store(out_off, Y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=imask[:, None])\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Host entry point.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef run(hidden_states, A, B, C, D, initial_states):\n    Bb, L, H, P = hidden_states.shape\n    N = 256\n    Q = 256\n    device = hidden_states.device\n\n    pad = (Q - L % Q) % Q\n    L_pad = L + pad\n    NC = L_pad // Q\n\n    BLOCK_M = 64\n    BLOCK_N = 64\n\n    states = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    states_out = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    final_state = torch.empty((Bb, H, P, N), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)\n    output = torch.empty((Bb, L, H * P), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)\n\n    # strides\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l = A.stride(0), A.stride(1), A.stride(2)\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p = hidden_states.stride()\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n = B.stride(0), B.stride(1), B.stride(3)\n    sC_b, sC_l, sC_n = C.stride(0), C.stride(1), C.stride(3)\n    sD_h = D.stride(0)\n    si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n = initial_states.stride()\n\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n = states.stride()\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n = states_out.stride()\n    sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n = final_state.stride()\n    sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp = output.stride()\n\n    # K2: chunk_state (recomputes cumsum inline)\n    _chunk_state_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, N // BLOCK_N)](\n        hidden_states, B, A, states,\n        sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n        sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,\n    )\n\n    # K3: state_passing (recomputes a_last inline)\n    _state_passing_kernel[(Bb, H, N // BLOCK_N)](\n        states, initial_states, states_out, final_state, A,\n        sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n        si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,\n        so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n        sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4,\n    )\n\n    # K4: chunk_scan (recomputes cumsum inline)\n    _chunk_scan_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, Q // BLOCK_M)](\n        C, B, hidden_states, A, states_out, D, output,\n        sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,\n        sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n        sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n        sD_h,\n        sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_M=BLOCK_M, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,\n    )\n\n    return output, final_state\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":28,"newStart":1,"newLines":33,"lines":[" \"\"\"L2/043 Mamba-2 chunk scan with segment sum — Triton solution."," ","-Candidate c002: Option-A 4-stage SSD, bf16 tensor-core matmuls (fp32 accumulation).","+Candidate c004: fuse the K1 cumsum kernel away (recompute in K2/K3/K4)."," ","-Change vs c001 (which RUNTIME_ERROR'd on all 5 workloads — a compile/launch failure,","-not algebra): every ``tl.dot`` now consumes **bf16 operands** with the default fp32","-accumulator, and the ``input_precision=\"ieee\"`` kwarg is removed. This (a) sidesteps any","-kwarg-compat issue on the installed Triton build and (b) halves dot-operand shared memory,","-which is the prime suspect for the c001 launch failure (fp32 [64,256]/[256,64] tiles in a","-pipelined loop overflow A800 SRAM). ``num_warps``/``num_stages`` are pinned to bound SRAM.","+Evidence driving this change: on c002 (5/5 PASS, geomean 10.64x) the per-workload","+timing vector shows the three 64-tile workloads (WL1/3/4) all sit at ~0.158 ms regardless","+of NC in {1,2,4} or B in {1,2,4}, while 192-tile=0.210 ms and 256-tile=0.254 ms. A linear","+fit ``time ≈ floor + slope·tiles`` gives floor ≈ 0.126 ms (~80% of the 64-tile runtime) and","+slope ≈ 0.5 us/tile — i.e. a large fixed overhead (4 kernel launches + the acum/alast DRAM","+round-trips) dominates the small cases. c003 already showed c002 is NOT bound by redundant","+G = C·Bᵀ matmul, so the right lever is cutting fixed overhead, not matmul FLOPs."," ","-Numerical note: the input tensors are natively bf16, so bf16 tensor-core inputs carry the","-same operand precision as the reference (which merely upcasts bf16→fp32 losslessly before","-matmul); products accumulate in fp32. All decays, cumsum, exp arguments, accumulators and","-the D residual stay in fp32; only ``output``/``final_state`` are cast to bf16 at the end.","+This candidate removes kernel K1 entirely: the per-chunk cumsum a[t] = cumsum_t A and its","+total a_last are recomputed inside K2, K3 and K4 (a[t] is a cheap 256-element scan). That","+deletes one launch and the ``acum:[B,H,NC,Q]`` + ``alast:[B,H,NC]`` DRAM tensors (read","+twice, written once). Algebra is unchanged and numerically identical to c002 (cumsum in","+fp32; padded rows load A=0 so the scan stays flat, matching the reference). In K4 the query","+/ key cumsum sub-blocks a_i / a_j are extracted from the full fp32 cumsum via an exact","+one-hot gather (a [BLOCK_M, Q] mask-and-sum, negligible next to the matmuls)."," ","+All decays / cumsum / exp / accumulators / D residual stay in fp32; bf16 only for","+tensor-core operands and the final output / final_state casts.","+"," Stages (all working intermediates in fp32; only output / final_state cast to bf16):","-  K1 chunk_cumsum   : a[t] = cumsum_t A over each chunk, plus a_last = a[Q-1].","-  K2 chunk_state    : states[p,n] = sum_t exp(a_last - a[t]) * X[t,p] * B[t,n].","-  K3 state_passing  : sequential inter-chunk recurrence seeded by initial_states,","+  K2 chunk_state    : a=cumsum(A); states[p,n] = sum_t exp(a_last - a[t]) * X[t,p] * B[t,n].","+  K3 state_passing  : a_last(c)=sum_t A; recurrence seeded by initial_states,","                       new_states[c+1] = exp(a_last(c)) * new_states[c] + states[c];","                       states_out[c] = new_states[c], final_state = new_states[NC].","-  K4 chunk_scan     : Y = (G∘L)·X  +  exp(a[t])·(C·states_out)  +  D[h]·X","-                      with G[i,j] = C_i·B_j (head-independent), L[i,j]=exp(a[i]-a[j]),","-                      lower-triangular; never materializes [Q,Q] to DRAM.","+  K4 chunk_scan     : a=cumsum(A); Y = (G∘L)·X + exp(a[t])·(C·states_out) + D[h]·X,","+                      G[i,j]=C_i·B_j, L[i,j]=exp(a[i]-a[j]) lower-tri; no [Q,Q] to DRAM."," "," Constants for this task: H=16, P=64, N=256, n_groups=1, Q(chunk)=256."," No Torch/CPU/NumPy computational fallback anywhere: Triton is the only compute path."]},{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":42,"newStart":39,"newLines":15,"lines":[" "," "," # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","-# K1: per-chunk inclusive cumsum of A, and per-chunk total (a_last).","-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","-@triton.jit","-def _cumsum_kernel(","-    A_ptr, acum_ptr, alast_ptr,","-    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","-    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,","-    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,","-    L,","-    Q: tl.constexpr,","-):","-    b = tl.program_id(0)","-    c = tl.program_id(1)","-    h = tl.program_id(2)","-","-    t = tl.arange(0, Q)","-    seq = c * Q + t","-    m = seq < L","-    a = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=m, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)","-    acum = tl.cumsum(a, axis=0)","-    tl.store(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + t * sac_q, acum)","-    last = tl.sum(a, axis=0)","-    tl.store(alast_ptr + b * sal_b + h * sal_h + c * sal_c, last)","-","-","-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"," # K2: per-(b,chunk,head) state = sum_t decay_state[t] * X[t,:] outer B[t,:].","-#     grid = (B*NC*H, N // BLOCK_N)","+#     grid = (B*NC*H, N // BLOCK_N).  Recomputes a = cumsum(A) inline."," # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"," @triton.jit"," def _chunk_state_kernel(","-    X_ptr, B_ptr, acum_ptr, alast_ptr, states_ptr,","+    X_ptr, B_ptr, A_ptr, states_ptr,","     sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,","     sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,","-    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,","-    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,","+    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","     sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,","     L, NC, H,","     Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,"]},{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":9,"newStart":65,"newLines":10,"lines":["     p = tl.arange(0, P)","     n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)"," ","-    acum = tl.load(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + t * sac_q).to(tl.float32)","-    alast = tl.load(alast_ptr + b * sal_b + h * sal_h + c * sal_c).to(tl.float32)","-    decay = tl.exp(alast - acum)  # [Q]","+    Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=tmask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)","+    acum = tl.cumsum(Arow, axis=0)          # [Q]","+    alast = tl.sum(Arow, axis=0)            # scalar","+    decay = tl.exp(alast - acum)            # [Q]"," ","     X = tl.load(","         X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + p[None, :] * sX_p,"]},{"oldStart":111,"oldLines":18,"newStart":90,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"," # K3: inter-chunk sequential recurrence. grid = (B, H, N // BLOCK_N).","-#     Elementwise in (p, n), so tiling over n is safe.","+#     Recomputes a_last(c) = sum_t A inline (no alast tensor)."," # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"," @triton.jit"," def _state_passing_kernel(","-    states_ptr, init_ptr, states_out_ptr, final_ptr, alast_ptr,","+    states_ptr, init_ptr, states_out_ptr, final_ptr, A_ptr,","     sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,","     si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,","     so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,","     sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,","-    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,","-    NC, H,","-    P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,","+    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","+    L, NC, H,","+    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,"," ):","     b = tl.program_id(0)","     h = tl.program_id(1)"]},{"oldStart":130,"oldLines":6,"newStart":109,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ","     p = tl.arange(0, P)","     n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)","+    t = tl.arange(0, Q)"," ","     state = tl.load(","         init_ptr + b * si_b + h * si_h + p[:, None] * si_p + n[None, :] * si_n"]},{"oldStart":140,"oldLines":8,"newStart":120,"newLines":10,"lines":["             states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + p[:, None] * so_p + n[None, :] * so_n,","             state,","         )","-        alast = tl.load(alast_ptr + b * sal_b + h * sal_h + c * sal_c).to(tl.float32)","-        g = tl.exp(alast)","+        seq = c * Q + t","+        smask = seq < L","+        Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=smask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)","+        g = tl.exp(tl.sum(Arow, axis=0))","         st = tl.load(","             states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n","         ).to(tl.float32)"]},{"oldStart":154,"oldLines":15,"newStart":136,"newLines":15,"lines":[" "," "," # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------","-# K4: chunk scan. grid = (B*NC*H, Q // BLOCK_M).","+# K4: chunk scan. grid = (B*NC*H, Q // BLOCK_M).  Recomputes a = cumsum(A) inline."," # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"," @triton.jit"," def _chunk_scan_kernel(","-    C_ptr, B_ptr, X_ptr, acum_ptr, states_out_ptr, D_ptr, out_ptr,","+    C_ptr, B_ptr, X_ptr, A_ptr, states_out_ptr, D_ptr, out_ptr,","     sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,","     sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,","     sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,","-    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,","+    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","     so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,","     sD_h,","     sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,"]},{"oldStart":176,"oldLines":13,"newStart":158,"newLines":21,"lines":["     c = rem // H","     h = rem % H"," ","+    qidx = tl.arange(0, Q)","+    seq_full = c * Q + qidx","+    fmask = seq_full < L","+    Arow = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq_full * sA_l, mask=fmask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)","+    a_full = tl.cumsum(Arow, axis=0)  # [Q]","+","     im = iblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)  # chunk-local query rows","     seq_i = c * Q + im","     imask = seq_i < L","     nidx = tl.arange(0, N)","     pidx = tl.arange(0, P)"," ","-    a_i = tl.load(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + im * sac_q).to(tl.float32)  # [BLOCK_M]","+    # exact gather a_i = a_full[im] via one-hot mask-sum","+    a_i = tl.sum(tl.where(qidx[None, :] == im[:, None], a_full[None, :], 0.0), axis=1)  # [BLOCK_M]","+","     C_i = tl.load(","         C_ptr + b * sC_b + seq_i[:, None] * sC_l + nidx[None, :] * sC_n,","         mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,"]},{"oldStart":194,"oldLines":7,"newStart":184,"newLines":7,"lines":["         jm = jblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)","         seq_j = c * Q + jm","         jmask = seq_j < L","-        a_j = tl.load(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + jm * sac_q).to(tl.float32)","+        a_j = tl.sum(tl.where(qidx[None, :] == jm[:, None], a_full[None, :], 0.0), axis=1)  # [BLOCK_M]","         B_j = tl.load(","             B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq_j[:, None] * sB_l + nidx[None, :] * sB_n,","             mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,"]},{"oldStart":246,"oldLines":8,"newStart":236,"newLines":6,"lines":["     BLOCK_M = 64","     BLOCK_N = 64"," ","-    acum = torch.empty((Bb, H, NC, Q), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)","-    alast = torch.empty((Bb, H, NC), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)","     states = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)","     states_out = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)","     final_state = torch.empty((Bb, H, P, N), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)"]},{"oldStart":261,"oldLines":54,"newStart":249,"newLines":41,"lines":["     sD_h = D.stride(0)","     si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n = initial_states.stride()"," ","-    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q = acum.stride()","-    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c = alast.stride()","     sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n = states.stride()","     so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n = states_out.stride()","     sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n = final_state.stride()","     sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp = output.stride()"," ","-    # K1: cumsum","-    _cumsum_kernel[(Bb, NC, H)](","-        A, acum, alast,","-        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","-        sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,","-        sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,","-        L,","-        Q=Q, num_warps=4,","-    )","-","-    # K2: chunk_state","+    # K2: chunk_state (recomputes cumsum inline)","     _chunk_state_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, N // BLOCK_N)](","-        hidden_states, B, acum, alast, states,","+        hidden_states, B, A, states,","         sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,","         sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,","-        sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,","-        sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,","+        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","         sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,","         L, NC, H,","         Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,","     )"," ","-    # K3: state_passing","+    # K3: state_passing (recomputes a_last inline)","     _state_passing_kernel[(Bb, H, N // BLOCK_N)](","-        states, initial_states, states_out, final_state, alast,","+        states, initial_states, states_out, final_state, A,","         sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,","         si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,","         so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,","         sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,","-        sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,","-        NC, H,","-        P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4,","+        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","+        L, NC, H,","+        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4,","     )"," ","-    # K4: chunk_scan","+    # K4: chunk_scan (recomputes cumsum inline)","     _chunk_scan_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, Q // BLOCK_M)](","-        C, B, hidden_states, acum, states_out, D, output,","+        C, B, hidden_states, A, states_out, D, output,","         sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,","         sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,","         sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,","-        sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,","+        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,","         so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,","         sD_h,","         sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,"]}],"originalFile":"\"\"\"L2/043 Mamba-2 chunk scan with segment sum — Triton solution.\n\nCandidate c002: Option-A 4-stage SSD, bf16 tensor-core matmuls (fp32 accumulation).\n\nChange vs c001 (which RUNTIME_ERROR'd on all 5 workloads — a compile/launch failure,\nnot algebra): every ``tl.dot`` now consumes **bf16 operands** with the default fp32\naccumulator, and the ``input_precision=\"ieee\"`` kwarg is removed. This (a) sidesteps any\nkwarg-compat issue on the installed Triton build and (b) halves dot-operand shared memory,\nwhich is the prime suspect for the c001 launch failure (fp32 [64,256]/[256,64] tiles in a\npipelined loop overflow A800 SRAM). ``num_warps``/``num_stages`` are pinned to bound SRAM.\n\nNumerical note: the input tensors are natively bf16, so bf16 tensor-core inputs carry the\nsame operand precision as the reference (which merely upcasts bf16→fp32 losslessly before\nmatmul); products accumulate in fp32. All decays, cumsum, exp arguments, accumulators and\nthe D residual stay in fp32; only ``output``/``final_state`` are cast to bf16 at the end.\n\nStages (all working intermediates in fp32; only output / final_state cast to bf16):\n  K1 chunk_cumsum   : a[t] = cumsum_t A over each chunk, plus a_last = a[Q-1].\n  K2 chunk_state    : states[p,n] = sum_t exp(a_last - a[t]) * X[t,p] * B[t,n].\n  K3 state_passing  : sequential inter-chunk recurrence seeded by initial_states,\n                      new_states[c+1] = exp(a_last(c)) * new_states[c] + states[c];\n                      states_out[c] = new_states[c], final_state = new_states[NC].\n  K4 chunk_scan     : Y = (G∘L)·X  +  exp(a[t])·(C·states_out)  +  D[h]·X\n                      with G[i,j] = C_i·B_j (head-independent), L[i,j]=exp(a[i]-a[j]),\n                      lower-triangular; never materializes [Q,Q] to DRAM.\n\nConstants for this task: H=16, P=64, N=256, n_groups=1, Q(chunk)=256.\nNo Torch/CPU/NumPy computational fallback anywhere: Triton is the only compute path.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K1: per-chunk inclusive cumsum of A, and per-chunk total (a_last).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _cumsum_kernel(\n    A_ptr, acum_ptr, alast_ptr,\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,\n    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,\n    L,\n    Q: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    b = tl.program_id(0)\n    c = tl.program_id(1)\n    h = tl.program_id(2)\n\n    t = tl.arange(0, Q)\n    seq = c * Q + t\n    m = seq < L\n    a = tl.load(A_ptr + b * sA_b + h * sA_h + seq * sA_l, mask=m, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n    acum = tl.cumsum(a, axis=0)\n    tl.store(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + t * sac_q, acum)\n    last = tl.sum(a, axis=0)\n    tl.store(alast_ptr + b * sal_b + h * sal_h + c * sal_c, last)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K2: per-(b,chunk,head) state = sum_t decay_state[t] * X[t,:] outer B[t,:].\n#     grid = (B*NC*H, N // BLOCK_N)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _chunk_state_kernel(\n    X_ptr, B_ptr, acum_ptr, alast_ptr, states_ptr,\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,\n    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    bch = tl.program_id(0)\n    nblk = tl.program_id(1)\n    b = bch // (NC * H)\n    rem = bch % (NC * H)\n    c = rem // H\n    h = rem % H\n\n    t = tl.arange(0, Q)\n    seq = c * Q + t\n    tmask = seq < L\n    p = tl.arange(0, P)\n    n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n\n    acum = tl.load(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + t * sac_q).to(tl.float32)\n    alast = tl.load(alast_ptr + b * sal_b + h * sal_h + c * sal_c).to(tl.float32)\n    decay = tl.exp(alast - acum)  # [Q]\n\n    X = tl.load(\n        X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + p[None, :] * sX_p,\n        mask=tmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    ).to(tl.float32)  # [Q, P]\n    Xd = (X * decay[:, None]).to(tl.bfloat16)  # [Q, P] bf16 (decay applied in fp32)\n\n    Bt = tl.load(\n        B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq[:, None] * sB_l + n[None, :] * sB_n,\n        mask=tmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    )  # [Q, BLOCK_N] bf16 (native)\n\n    states = tl.dot(tl.trans(Xd), Bt)  # [P, BLOCK_N] fp32 accumulate\n    tl.store(\n        states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n,\n        states,\n    )\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K3: inter-chunk sequential recurrence. grid = (B, H, N // BLOCK_N).\n#     Elementwise in (p, n), so tiling over n is safe.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _state_passing_kernel(\n    states_ptr, init_ptr, states_out_ptr, final_ptr, alast_ptr,\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n    si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n    sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,\n    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,\n    NC, H,\n    P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    b = tl.program_id(0)\n    h = tl.program_id(1)\n    nblk = tl.program_id(2)\n\n    p = tl.arange(0, P)\n    n = nblk * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n\n    state = tl.load(\n        init_ptr + b * si_b + h * si_h + p[:, None] * si_p + n[None, :] * si_n\n    ).to(tl.float32)  # [P, BLOCK_N]\n\n    for c in range(0, NC):\n        tl.store(\n            states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + p[:, None] * so_p + n[None, :] * so_n,\n            state,\n        )\n        alast = tl.load(alast_ptr + b * sal_b + h * sal_h + c * sal_c).to(tl.float32)\n        g = tl.exp(alast)\n        st = tl.load(\n            states_ptr + b * sst_b + c * sst_c + h * sst_h + p[:, None] * sst_p + n[None, :] * sst_n\n        ).to(tl.float32)\n        state = g * state + st\n\n    tl.store(\n        final_ptr + b * sf_b + h * sf_h + p[:, None] * sf_p + n[None, :] * sf_n,\n        state.to(tl.bfloat16),\n    )\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# K4: chunk scan. grid = (B*NC*H, Q // BLOCK_M).\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@triton.jit\ndef _chunk_scan_kernel(\n    C_ptr, B_ptr, X_ptr, acum_ptr, states_out_ptr, D_ptr, out_ptr,\n    sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n    sD_h,\n    sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,\n    L, NC, H,\n    Q: tl.constexpr, P: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    bch = tl.program_id(0)\n    iblk = tl.program_id(1)\n    b = bch // (NC * H)\n    rem = bch % (NC * H)\n    c = rem // H\n    h = rem % H\n\n    im = iblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)  # chunk-local query rows\n    seq_i = c * Q + im\n    imask = seq_i < L\n    nidx = tl.arange(0, N)\n    pidx = tl.arange(0, P)\n\n    a_i = tl.load(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + im * sac_q).to(tl.float32)  # [BLOCK_M]\n    C_i = tl.load(\n        C_ptr + b * sC_b + seq_i[:, None] * sC_l + nidx[None, :] * sC_n,\n        mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    )  # [BLOCK_M, N] bf16\n\n    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, P), dtype=tl.float32)\n\n    for jblk in range(0, iblk + 1):\n        jm = jblk * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\n        seq_j = c * Q + jm\n        jmask = seq_j < L\n        a_j = tl.load(acum_ptr + b * sac_b + h * sac_h + c * sac_c + jm * sac_q).to(tl.float32)\n        B_j = tl.load(\n            B_ptr + b * sB_b + seq_j[:, None] * sB_l + nidx[None, :] * sB_n,\n            mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n        )  # [BLOCK_M, N] bf16\n        X_j = tl.load(\n            X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq_j[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + pidx[None, :] * sX_p,\n            mask=jmask[:, None], other=0.0,\n        )  # [BLOCK_M, P] bf16\n\n        G = tl.dot(C_i, tl.trans(B_j))  # [BLOCK_M, BLOCK_M] fp32\n        diff = a_i[:, None] - a_j[None, :]\n        cmask = im[:, None] >= jm[None, :]\n        Lm = tl.where(cmask, tl.exp(diff), 0.0)\n        M = (G * Lm).to(tl.bfloat16)\n        acc += tl.dot(M, X_j)\n\n    states_o = tl.load(\n        states_out_ptr + b * so_b + c * so_c + h * so_h + pidx[:, None] * so_p + nidx[None, :] * so_n\n    ).to(tl.bfloat16)  # [P, N]\n    Cstate = tl.dot(C_i, tl.trans(states_o))  # [BLOCK_M, P] fp32\n    a_i_exp = tl.exp(a_i)\n    Y = acc + a_i_exp[:, None] * Cstate\n\n    X_i = tl.load(\n        X_ptr + b * sX_b + seq_i[:, None] * sX_l + h * sX_h + pidx[None, :] * sX_p,\n        mask=imask[:, None], other=0.0,\n    ).to(tl.float32)\n    Dh = tl.load(D_ptr + h * sD_h).to(tl.float32)\n    Y = Y + Dh * X_i\n\n    out_off = out_ptr + b * sout_b + seq_i[:, None] * sout_l + (h * P + pidx[None, :]) * sout_hp\n    tl.store(out_off, Y.to(tl.bfloat16), mask=imask[:, None])\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Host entry point.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef run(hidden_states, A, B, C, D, initial_states):\n    Bb, L, H, P = hidden_states.shape\n    N = 256\n    Q = 256\n    device = hidden_states.device\n\n    pad = (Q - L % Q) % Q\n    L_pad = L + pad\n    NC = L_pad // Q\n\n    BLOCK_M = 64\n    BLOCK_N = 64\n\n    acum = torch.empty((Bb, H, NC, Q), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    alast = torch.empty((Bb, H, NC), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    states = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    states_out = torch.empty((Bb, NC, H, P, N), dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    final_state = torch.empty((Bb, H, P, N), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)\n    output = torch.empty((Bb, L, H * P), dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=device)\n\n    # strides\n    sA_b, sA_h, sA_l = A.stride(0), A.stride(1), A.stride(2)\n    sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p = hidden_states.stride()\n    sB_b, sB_l, sB_n = B.stride(0), B.stride(1), B.stride(3)\n    sC_b, sC_l, sC_n = C.stride(0), C.stride(1), C.stride(3)\n    sD_h = D.stride(0)\n    si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n = initial_states.stride()\n\n    sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q = acum.stride()\n    sal_b, sal_h, sal_c = alast.stride()\n    sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n = states.stride()\n    so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n = states_out.stride()\n    sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n = final_state.stride()\n    sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp = output.stride()\n\n    # K1: cumsum\n    _cumsum_kernel[(Bb, NC, H)](\n        A, acum, alast,\n        sA_b, sA_h, sA_l,\n        sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,\n        sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,\n        L,\n        Q=Q, num_warps=4,\n    )\n\n    # K2: chunk_state\n    _chunk_state_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, N // BLOCK_N)](\n        hidden_states, B, acum, alast, states,\n        sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n        sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n        sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,\n        sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,\n        sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,\n    )\n\n    # K3: state_passing\n    _state_passing_kernel[(Bb, H, N // BLOCK_N)](\n        states, initial_states, states_out, final_state, alast,\n        sst_b, sst_c, sst_h, sst_p, sst_n,\n        si_b, si_h, si_p, si_n,\n        so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n        sf_b, sf_h, sf_p, sf_n,\n        sal_b, sal_h, sal_c,\n        NC, H,\n        P=P, N=N, BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N, num_warps=4,\n    )\n\n    # K4: chunk_scan\n    _chunk_scan_kernel[(Bb * NC * H, Q // BLOCK_M)](\n        C, B, hidden_states, acum, states_out, D, output,\n        sC_b, sC_l, sC_n,\n        sB_b, sB_l, sB_n,\n        sX_b, sX_l, sX_h, sX_p,\n        sac_b, sac_h, sac_c, sac_q,\n        so_b, so_c, so_h, so_p, so_n,\n        sD_h,\n        sout_b, sout_l, sout_hp,\n        L, NC, H,\n        Q=Q, P=P, N=N, BLOCK_M=BLOCK_M, num_warps=4, num_stages=2,\n    )\n\n    return output, final_state\n","userModified":false}}
