{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0bfec376-c561-4e25-97c7-f7f4302fd8d8","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XRygUiwqZ9rvRSxRhrRhZy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/candidates.jsonl","content":"{\"candidate_id\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c002\", \"source_sha256\": \"8604925adcacd4247f245ebe23f97fdf253bf2049b546e05bf44e1782973a955\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T01:30:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"c002 per-workload timing suggests a large fixed overhead dominates the small (64-tile) cases (all ~0.158ms regardless of NC/B). Remove kernel K1 (chunk_cumsum) and its acum/alast DRAM tensors by recomputing a=cumsum(A) inline inside K2/K3/K4; expect lower launch+DRAM overhead, especially on WL1/3/4.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"Deleted K1 and the acum:[B,H,NC,Q]/alast:[B,H,NC] tensors. K2 computes acum=cumsum(A), alast=sum(A) inline; K3 computes g=exp(sum(A)) per chunk inline; K4 computes a_full=cumsum(A) over the full Q and extracts a_i/a_j sub-blocks via one-hot mask-sum gathers. Algebra numerically identical to c002.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (cumsum axis/padding/exp-order identical to c002; one-hot gather a_i=sum(where(q==im,a_full)) exact)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 7.912875213740715, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.208781}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 7.996020196859037, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.3894665}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 7.8974903265166265, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.1794855}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 7.786195396643158, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.18291}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 6.769548762452112, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.4094185}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 7.65801943560213, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 7.6724259792423295, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS but geomean 7.66x REGRESSES vs c002's 10.64x (-28%). Removing K1 was a net loss: the inline recompute cost (a full Q=256 cumsum PLUS a [BLOCK_M,Q]=[64,256] one-hot gather per i-block in K4, repeated across all B*NC*H*(Q/BLOCK_M) programs) vastly exceeds the single cheap K1 launch + tiny acum/alast round-trip it replaced. Compute-heavy WL2/WL5 collapsed (12.25->8.00, 13.23->6.77) because K4 now redoes the cumsum+gather work per i-block; even the 64-tile cases got worse (K1 was NOT the fixed-overhead culprit). Revert to c002.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 4, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Lessons so far: (c003) materializing G to DRAM hurts; (c004) inline cumsum recompute hurts and K1 is cheap. Both point to c002 being memory/launch-tuned already, NOT matmul- or K1-bound. The real large tensors are states/states_out:[B,NC,H,P,N] fp32 (~268MB each for WL2, ~1GB round-trip). Next c005: keep c002 structure but store states & states_out in bf16 to halve that traffic. Low risk numerically: K4 already casts states_out->bf16 before the C.states dot (so the off-diagonal term is bit-identical), and K3 accumulates the recurrence in fp32 with only the per-chunk increment rounded to bf16 (NC<=4 additions, well within rtol=0.05). Reverting solution.py to c002 for the c005 branch.\"}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":115429,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6fba2c0-4823-4806-9479-4c36036ed424","uuid":"a556370b-21f7-46c0-a82f-39fe4b2c6fff","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:07:57.983Z"}
