": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.21968448208945, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.219005, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 9.360167197136782, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.151438, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 9.37955584241099, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.151838, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.54705944101824, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.190525, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 11.490600605016208, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 11.707361201, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS; geomean 11.49x, up from c002's 10.64x (+8%). New best and parent. Every workload improved (WL1 10.49->11.03, WL2 12.25->14.22, WL3 8.97->9.36, WL4 8.94->9.38, WL5 13.23->14.55). Confirms the states/states_out fp32 round-trip was a real bottleneck; bf16 storage halves it with no correctness loss (max_abs/max_rel identical to c002).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 5, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Compute-heavy WL2/WL5 gained most (~+2 speedup), consistent with them having the largest states tensors. 64-tile WL3/WL4 still ~9.4x, launch/occupancy-limited. Next c006: attack the 64-tile floor by exposing more grid parallelism, OR try the acum tensor in bf16 too. Prefer the occupancy lever for WL3/WL4.\"}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":150510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_token