{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwkYmKwQL1BX8NggLpcSoQ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/candidates.jsonl has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6fba2c0-4823-4806-9479-4c36036ed424","uuid":"c69e9062-989f-4302-a8cc-ad8c529f009c","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:13:54.118Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/candidates.jsonl","oldString":"Reverting solution.py to c002 for the c005 branch.\"}","newString":"Reverting solution.py to c002 for the c005 branch.\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c002\", \"source_sha256\": \"4dbc6b46eeef0a575fb3892dedbf3585948fbf7ccf44cb0940e3ae507170ee6b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T02:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"c002 is memory/launch-lean but still round-trips the large states/states_out:[B,NC,H,P,N] fp32 tensors (~0.27GB each on WL2). Store both in bf16 to halve that DRAM traffic; compute stays fp32. K4 already cast states_out->bf16 before the C.states dot (off-diagonal bit-identical); K3 recurrence stays fp32 in-register with only the per-chunk increment bf16-rounded (NC<=4 adds, <<rtol). Expect a uniform speedup.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"states and states_out tensors allocated bf16 (was fp32); K2 stores states.to(bf16); K3 stores state.to(bf16) for states_out and carries state in fp32 registers; K4 loads states_out as bf16 directly (removed the redundant .to(bf16)). All arithmetic still fp32.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (only intermediate storage dtype changed; recurrence/decay/exp/accumulators all fp32; off-diagonal term numerically identical to c002)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79