3). K2 now takes A + acum/alast pointers, computes acum=cumsum(A)/alast=sum(A) inline, and stores them when nblk==0. K3/K4 unchanged (still read acum/alast from DRAM). states/states_out remain bf16. All arithmetic fp32; numerics identical to c005.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (cumsum/padding/exp-order identical to c005; nblk==0 guard stores acum/alast exactly once per (b,chunk,head); N//BLOCK_N=4 programs share the same cumsum so the stored value is well-defined)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.382918707149852, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.1148625, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 16.796645182168767, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.185405, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 12.083240985423238, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.11731, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 12.148485249145912, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.1172305, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.774048635961368, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.155934, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 14.451465, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 14.637067, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS; geomean 14.45x, up from c005's 11.49x (+26%). New best and parent. Every workload improved substantially (WL1 11.03->14.38, WL2 14.22->16.80, WL3 9.36->12.08, WL4 9.38->12.15, WL5 14.55->17.77). Folding K1 into K2 removed a full launch + A-read and the small workloads gained most (WL1 +30%, WL3/WL4 +29%), confirming the floor was launch/overhead-bound. max_abs/max_rel identical to c005 => numerics unchanged. Contrast with c004: recomputing cumsum in K4 was fatal, but computing it once in K2 and storing is a clear win.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 6, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Now 3 launches (K2,K3,K4). K3 is tiny (grid B*H*4, NC<=4 sequential) and a candidate to fold into K2 or K4, but the inter-chunk recurrence is sequential over chunks so it cannot trivially merge with the per-(b,chunk) K2/K4. Next c007: try folding K3 into K4 via a single (b,h)-serial mega-kernel that loops chunks carrying state in registers (Option C) to drop another launch + the states/states_out round-trip; risk = serializing chunks & lower parallelism on WL3/WL4. Alternatively micro-tune num_warps/BLOCK_N on K2. c006 is a strong best; remaining gains likely smaller.\"}","+{\"candidate_id\": \"c007\", \"parent\": \"c006\", \"source_sha256\": \"215f96fd287cbd2aff4a70d0b7471dc9dc98422f7fb44da67e99547f8962fa37\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T03:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Fuse K2 (chunk_state) and K3 (state_passing) into one kernel KS (grid B,H,N/BLOCK_N) that carries the [P,BLOCK_N] state in fp32 registers and loops chunks: store states_out[c]=carried state, compute contrib via bf16 dot, state=exp(a_last)*state+contrib. Removes the entire 'states' intermediate tensor AND one launch (3->2). acum still persisted for K4. Expect a further speedup; risk is losing NC-fold parallelism in the state stage (bites B=1 WL4 only).\", \"change_from_parent\": \"Deleted K2 and K3, replaced by fused _state_pass_kernel; removed the states:[B,NC,H,P,N] tensor and the alast tensor. Per-chunk contrib now stays fp32 in-register (no bf16 round-trip through states), marginally more accurate. acum persisted by nblk==0 program. K4 unchanged. Launches 3->2.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (states_out[c] stored BEFORE the chunk-c update = state from chunks<c, matching reference states_with_init recurrence; final_state=state after last chunk; cumsum/decay/exp-order identical to c006; acum stored once per (b,chunk,head))\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 20.246056936972266, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.081599, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 19.79042692459233, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.157358, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.03073374103399, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.083231, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.07498171616291, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.083407, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 22.596723302949762, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.122654, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 19.234813, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 19.347784, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS; geomean 19.23x, up from c006's 14.45x (+33%). New best and parent. Every workload jumped (WL1 14.38->20.25, WL2 16.80->19.79, WL3 12.08->17.03, WL4 12.15->17.07, WL5 17.77->22.60). Fusing K2+K3 removed a launch AND the entire states:[B,NC,H,P,N] bf16 round-trip; the feared serialization on WL4 (B=1, NC=4) did NOT hurt -- WL4 still gained +40%, so on A800 the removed round-trip/launch dominates the lost NC parallelism. max_abs/max_rel identical to c006 => numerics preserved (register-fp32 contrib is >= as accurate).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 7, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Now 2 launches (KS, K4) and only acum + states_out cross DRAM between them. Cumulative arc: c002 10.64 -> c005 11.49 -> c006 14.45 -> c007 19.23. Remaining ideas: (a) also fuse acum away by having K4 recompute cumsum ONCE per (b,chunk,head) in a cheap form -- but c004 showed per-i-block recompute is fatal, so would need a single-i-block K4 (BLOCK_M=Q=256) to amortize; (b) micro-tune num_warps in {2,8} / BLOCK_N in {128,256} for KS and K4; (c) collapse K4's states_out read by fusing the off-diagonal into KS. Diminishing returns likely; next c008 = try BLOCK_M=128 or num_warps sweep on K4 (single knob).\"}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3c80f9a9-d924-43bf-8389-82d67f511b2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018bMRvzCvxAugEQYvPHTYG4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-043_mamba_chunk_scan_with_segsum/docs/plan.md","old_string":"  c006 is already a strong best.\n\n## 9. Immediate next action (next turn, not now)","new_string":"  c006 is already a strong best.\n\n- **c007 (eval #7) — ACCEPT (new best/parent).** Fused K2 (chunk_state) + K3\n  (state_passing) into one kernel `KS` (grid `(B,H,N/BLOCK_N)`) that carries the\n  `[P,BLOCK_N]` SSM state in fp32 registers and loops chunks: store `states_out[c]` =\n  carried-in state, compute `contrib` via bf16 dot, `state = exp(a_last)·state + contrib`.\n  This removed the entire `states:[B,NC,H,P,N]` intermediate tensor *and* a launch (3→2).\n  Result: **5/5 PASS, geomean 19.23× vs c006's 14.45× (+33%)**, every workload up (WL1\n  14.38→20.25, WL2 16.80→19.79, WL3 12.08→17.03, WL4 12.15→17.07, WL5 17.77→22.60). The\n  feared chunk serialization on WL4 (B=1, NC=4) did **not** bite — WL4 still gained +40%,\n  so the removed round-trip/launch dominates the lost NC-parallelism on A800.\n  `max_abs`/`max_rel` identical to c006 (the register-fp32 `contrib` is at least as\n  accurate). Cumulative arc: c002 10.64 → c005 11.49 → c006 14.45 → **c007 19.23**.\n  **Next (c008):** only 2 launches remain (KS, K4); `acum` + `states_out` are the only\n  cross-kernel DRAM. Diminishing returns expected. Try single-knob micro-tuning first\n  (`BLOCK_M`∈{128,256} or `num_warps`∈{2,8} on K4); larger structural ideas (fuse `acum`\n  away — needs single-i-block K4 to avoid c004's fatal per-i-block recompute; or fold the\n  off-diagonal into KS) are higher-risk.\n\n## 9. Immediate next action (next turn, not now)"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_t