Wiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Now 3 launches (K2,K3,K4). K3 is tiny (grid B*H*4, NC<=4 sequential) and a candidate to fold into K2 or K4, but the inter-chunk recurrence is sequential over chunks so it cannot trivially merge with the per-(b,chunk) K2/K4. Next c007: try folding K3 into K4 via a single (b,h)-serial mega-kernel that loops chunks carrying state in registers (Option C) to drop another launch + the states/states_out round-trip; risk = serializing chunks & lower parallelism on WL3/WL4. Alternatively micro-tune num_warps/BLOCK_N on K2. c006 is a strong best; remaining gains likely smaller.\"}"," {\"candidate_id\": \"c007\", \"parent\": \"c006\", \"source_sha256\": \"215f96fd287cbd2aff4a70d0b7471dc9dc98422f7fb44da67e99547f8962fa37\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T03:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Fuse K2 (chunk_state) and K3 (state_passing) into one kernel KS (grid B,H,N/BLOCK_N) that carries the [P,BLOCK_N] state in fp32 registers and loops chunks: store states_out[c]=carried state, compute contrib via bf16 dot, state=exp(a_last)*state+contrib. Removes the entire 'states' intermediate tensor AND one launch (3->2). acum still persisted for K4. Expect a further speedup; risk is losing NC-fold parallelism in the state stage (bites B=1 WL4 only).\", \"change_from_parent\": \"Deleted K2 and K3, replaced by fused _state_pass_kernel; removed the states:[B,NC,H,P,N] tensor and the alast tensor. Per-chunk contrib now stays fp32 in-register (no bf16 round-trip through states), marginally more accurate. acum persisted by nblk==0 program. K4 unchanged. Launches 3->2.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (states_out[c] stored BEFORE the chunk-c update = state from chunks<c, matching reference states_with_init recurrence; final_state=state after last chunk; cumsum/decay/exp-order identical to c006; acum stored once per (b,chunk,head))\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 20.246056936972266, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.081599, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 19.79042692459233, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.157358, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.03073374103399, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.083231, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.07498171616291, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.083407, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 22.596723302949762, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.122654, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 19.234813, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 19.347784, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS; geomean 19.23x, up from c006's 14.45x (+33%). New best and parent. Every workload jumped (WL1 14.38->20.25, WL2 16.80->19.79, WL3 12.08->17.03, WL4 12.15->17.07, WL5 17.77->22.60). Fusing K2+K3 removed a launch AND the entire states:[B,NC,H,P,N] bf16 round-trip; the feared serialization on WL4 (B=1, NC=4) did NOT hurt -- WL4 still gained +40%, so on A800 the removed round-trip/launch dominates the lost NC parallelism. max_abs/max_rel identical to c006 => numerics preserved (register-fp32 contrib is >= as accurate).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 7, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Now 2 launches (KS, K4) and only acum + states_out cross DRAM between them. Cumulative arc: c002 10.64 -> c005 11.49 -> c006 14.45 -> c007 19.23. Remaining ideas: (a) also fuse acum away by having K4 recompute cumsum ONCE per (b,chunk,head) in a cheap form -- but c004 showed per-i-block recompute is fatal, so would need a single-i-block K4 (BLOCK_M=Q=256) to amortize; (b) micro-tune num_warps in {2,8} / BLOCK_N in {128,256} for KS and K4; (c) collapse K4's states_out read by fusing the off-diagonal into KS. Diminishing returns likely; next c008 = try BLOCK_M=128 or num_warps sweep on K4 (single knob).\"}"," {\"candidate_id\": \"c008\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"9aaf142378daa099a14c31327a3d681eebed6a5489093b819251fe2fba6ae20e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T03:30:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Single-knob micro-tune: K4 query-block BLOCK_M 64->128 for larger, more tensor-core-efficient tiles and a shorter lower-tri j-loop. Grid 2nd dim Q/BLOCK_M 4->2; even 64-tile workloads keep 64*2=128 programs > 108 SMs. KS untouched.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"BLOCK_M = 64 -> 128 in run(); K4 kernel body unchanged (masks/lower-tri already parameterized by BLOCK_M). Nothing else changed vs c007.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (lower-tri im>=jm mask and partial-row masks correct at 128 rows; a_i/a_j gathers over 128 rows valid; numerics identical to c007)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 16.512901500802126, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.1000465, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 13.911727785645043, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.223853, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 13.460117747602318, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.10531, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 13.369252576835702, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.106526, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 16.74325818260901, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.165534, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 14.724524, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 14.799451, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS but geomean 14.72x REGRESSES vs c007's 19.23x (-23%). BLOCK_M=128 hurt every workload (WL1 20.25->16.51, WL2 19.79->13.91, WL3 17.03->13.46, WL4 17.07->13.37, WL5 22.60->16.74). The larger [128,N] tiles raise register/SRAM pressure and lower occupancy/pipelining more than the shorter j-loop saves; the extra grid parallelism from BLOCK_M=64 (Q/BLOCK_M=4) matters more on A800 than tile efficiency here (K4 tiles are tiny, P=64). BLOCK_M=64 (c007) is optimal for K4. Revert to c007.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 8, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"BLOCK_M=64 confirmed best. Reverting solution.py to c007. Remaining single knobs to try: num_warps in {2,8} on K4 or KS (c009), num_stages in {3,4}, BLOCK_N in {128,256} on KS. Given c008 (tile size) regressed and structural fusion is exhausted (2 launches, minimal DRAM), gains are likely <2%; one or two more targeted knob candidates then converge.\"}","+{\"candidate_id\": \"c009\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"fc01cffec3050cbc5364c41aa440064511bf2a44e642216483a8f2226559f2f1\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T04:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Single-knob micro-tune: K4 num_warps 4 -> 8. K4's matmuls have a 256-long contraction (C.B^T, C.states) that could use more warps for the reduction; K4 has >=256 programs so occupancy should hold. KS untouched.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"K4 launch num_warps 4 -> 8. BLOCK_M stays 64. Nothing else changed vs c007.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (launch param only; kernel body & numerics identical to c007)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.209116761632934, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.095999, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 13.160192954172327, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.2366365, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.218286866376783, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.0996945, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.264696160818918, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.099839, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 15.513666080804235, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.178654, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 14.810475943999162, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 14.87319176476104, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS but geomean 14.81x REGRESSES vs c007's 19.23x (-23%). num_warps=8 hurt every workload (WL1 20.25->17.21, WL2 19.79->13.16, WL3 17.03->14.22, WL4 17.07->14.26, WL5 22.60->15.51). K4's tiles are tiny (BLOCK_M=64, P=64 output), so 8 warps oversubscribe the small [64,64]/[64,256] dots and waste warps on too-small tiles, cutting per-SM occupancy. num_warps=4 (c007) is optimal for K4. Revert to c007.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 9, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Both tile-size (c008 BLOCK_M=128) and warp-count (c009 num_warps=8) micro-tunes on K4 regressed ~-23% -- c007's K4 config (BLOCK_M=64, num_warps=4, num_stages=2) is a local optimum. Two independent knob directions both worsened, and all structural fusion is exhausted (2 launches KS/K4, only acum+states_out cross DRAM, states materialization removed). Search has converged: c007 (geomean 19.23x, 5/5 pass) is the best valid candidate. Reverting solution.py to c007; next turn create SEARCH_COMPLETE unless a genuinely new lever appears.\"}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
