\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.106526, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 16.74325818260901, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.165534, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 14.724524, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 14.799451, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS but geomean 14.72x REGRESSES vs c007's 19.23x (-23%). BLOCK_M=128 hurt every workload (WL1 20.25->16.51, WL2 19.79->13.91, WL3 17.03->13.46, WL4 17.07->13.37, WL5 22.60->16.74). The larger [128,N] tiles raise register/SRAM pressure and lower occupancy/pipelining more than the shorter j-loop saves; the extra grid parallelism from BLOCK_M=64 (Q/BLOCK_M=4) matters more on A800 than tile efficiency here (K4 tiles are tiny, P=64). BLOCK_M=64 (c007) is optimal for K4. Revert to c007.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 8, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"BLOCK_M=64 confirmed best. Reverting solution.py to c007. Remaining single knobs to try: num_warps in {2,8} on K4 or KS (c009), num_stages in {3,4}, BLOCK_N in {128,256} on KS. Given c008 (tile size) regressed and structural fusion is exhausted (2 launches, minimal DRAM), gains are likely <2%; one or two more targeted knob candidates then converge.\"}"," {\"candidate_id\": \"c009\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"fc01cffec3050cbc5364c41aa440064511bf2a44e642216483a8f2226559f2f1\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T04:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Single-knob micro-tune: K4 num_warps 4 -> 8. K4's matmuls have a 256-long contraction (C.B^T, C.states) that could use more warps for the reduction; K4 has >=256 programs so occupancy should hold. KS untouched.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"K4 launch num_warps 4 -> 8. BLOCK_M stays 64. Nothing else changed vs c007.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (launch param only; kernel body & numerics identical to c007)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.209116761632934, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.095999, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 13.160192954172327, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.2366365, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.218286866376783, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.0996945, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 14.264696160818918, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.099839, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 15.513666080804235, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.178654, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 14.810475943999162, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 14.87319176476104, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS but geomean 14.81x REGRESSES vs c007's 19.23x (-23%). num_warps=8 hurt every workload (WL1 20.25->17.21, WL2 19.79->13.16, WL3 17.03->14.22, WL4 17.07->14.26, WL5 22.60->15.51). K4's tiles are tiny (BLOCK_M=64, P=64 output), so 8 warps oversubscribe the small [64,64]/[64,256] dots and waste warps on too-small tiles, cutting per-SM occupancy. num_warps=4 (c007) is optimal for K4. Revert to c007.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 9, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Both tile-size (c008 BLOCK_M=128) and warp-count (c009 num_warps=8) micro-tunes on K4 regressed ~-23% -- c007's K4 config (BLOCK_M=64, num_warps=4, num_stages=2) is a local optimum. Two independent knob directions both worsened, and all structural fusion is exhausted (2 launches KS/K4, only acum+states_out cross DRAM, states materialization removed). Search has converged: c007 (geomean 19.23x, 5/5 pass) is the best valid candidate. Reverting solution.py to c007; next turn create SEARCH_COMPLETE unless a genuinely new lever appears.\"}","+{\"candidate_id\": \"c010\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"49c407e4262b3f1768b4ffd56fe91f4ebf1f0b948a97e692f9f345ce679b4a9d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T04:30:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"K4 knob tunes preferred fewer resources; apply the lesson to KS: num_warps 4 -> 2 to free SM resources for more concurrent KS blocks on the low-occupancy B=1 case (WL4 KS grid only 64 programs). Expect WL3/WL4 to lift without hurting B=4.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"KS launch num_warps 4 -> 2. K4 untouched (num_warps=4). Nothing else changed vs c007.\", \"validation\": {\"static_checks\": \"pass (launch param only; kernel body & numerics identical to c007)\", \"harness_stage\": \"feedback\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"4bf2c843-37b5-5bcc-8809-79651bc70a27\", \"B\": 2, \"L\": 293, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 20.163031671446877, \"ref_ms\": 1.652058, \"sol_ms\": 0.081935, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.9835205078125}, {\"uuid\": \"2907639d-da31-514e-aad2-1a90f808b3ad\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 16.574936796444636, \"ref_ms\": 3.114182, \"sol_ms\": 0.187885, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 4.748114585876465}, {\"uuid\": \"a85c5733-0c73-556f-8514-570137ce6445\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 3.0045147683796647, \"ref_ms\": 1.417485, \"sol_ms\": 0.471785, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 10.30731201171875}, {\"uuid\": \"6dc47920-87cb-522b-be70-75445f3d5ec2\", \"B\": 1, \"L\": 1024, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 17.042391388893872, \"ref_ms\": 1.424173, \"sol_ms\": 0.0835665, \"max_abs\": 1.0, \"max_rel\": 5.839954853057861}, {\"uuid\": \"5fd24475-8733-54c5-9b2f-b4c6e85c6346\", \"B\": 4, \"L\": 541, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"passed\": true, \"speedup\": 19.531569211254208, \"ref_ms\": 2.7715785, \"sol_ms\": 0.1419025, \"max_abs\": 2.0, \"max_rel\": 5.1437907218933105}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 12.729548, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 15.263289, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"decision_reason\": \"5/5 PASS but geomean 12.73x REGRESSES vs c007's 19.23x. Catastrophic outlier on WL3 (B4,L256): 17.03x -> 3.00x (sol 0.083ms -> 0.472ms, ~5.7x slower). WL1/WL2/WL4/WL5 stayed ~flat/slightly down (20.25->20.16, 19.79->16.57, 17.07->17.04, 22.60->19.53). num_warps=2 on KS cripples the single-chunk NC=1 case (WL3): with only 2 warps the [64,64]-output dot over K=256 and the Q=256 cumsum are severely under-parallelized within each of the 256 KS programs, and the recurrence loop has no NC>1 amortization there. num_warps=4 (c007) is optimal for KS. Revert to c007.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 10, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not_used (A800=sm_80 Ampere; skill scope is Blackwell/Hopper)\"}, \"notes\": \"Third consecutive rejected micro-tune (c008 K4 BLOCK_M, c009 K4 num_warps, c010 KS num_warps). All three launch/tile knobs around c007 are at their optimum; moving any of them in either explored direction regresses (num_warps: 2 worse, 8 worse => 4 optimal; BLOCK_M: 128 worse => 64 optimal). Structural fusion fully exhausted (2 launches, states materialization removed, [Q,Q] never in DRAM, bf16 operands + fp32 accum). SEARCH CONVERGED: c007 (geomean 19.23x, 5/5 pass) is the best valid candidate. Reverting solution.py to c007 and creating SEARCH_COMPLETE next; no further justified candidate remains.\"}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
