regressed (−23%): oversubscribes the small dots.\n- c010 — KS `num_warps` 4→2 regressed (WL3 collapsed 17.03×→3.00×): under-parallelizes the single-chunk case.\n\nBoth `num_warps` directions (2 and 8) and the tile-size direction (128) worsen the result, confirming c007's launch config is a local optimum. Structurally the kernel already: never materializes the `[Q,Q]` score matrices to DRAM, has the minimal 2-kernel launch count (KS + K4), carries the inter-chunk state in fp32 registers, exploits the n_groups=1 head-sharing implicitly, and uses bf16 tensor-core operands with fp32 accumulation — while every selected workload passes correctness with unchanged `max_abs`/`max_rel`.\n\nThree consecutive rejected candidates and no remaining justified lever (structural fusion complete; all launch/tile knobs at optimum; precision already at the correctness-safe bf16/fp32 boundary) satisfy the plan's convergence criterion (§6.1/§6.3).\n\n## Budget status\n- Cumulative evaluations: **10 / 100**.\n- No `final` (16-workload) evaluation run — awaiting explicit operator approval per task rules.\n\n## Notes\n- `solution/solution.py` holds the best valid candidate (c007), hash verified.\n- `candidates.jsonl` contains the complete, append-only lineage c001–c010.\n- Skill usage: `KernelWiki` not used — its scope is Blackwell (SM100) / Hopper (SM90); this task targets A800 / sm_80 (Ampere), out of scope.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":219288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6fba2c0-4823-4806-9479-4c36036ed424","uuid":"a3a89765-ba1d-4a0a-81b6-bfac812ffa67","timestamp":"2026-09-17T21:45:36.562Z"}
